---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHead from '../../../components/sections/SectionHead.astro';

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Retail and Textile RFID Solutions",
  "provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Altis Technology" },
  "serviceType": "Retail and textile RFID automation",
  "areaServed": "TR",
  "description": "RFID, inventory accuracy, store counting, and omnichannel visibility solutions for retail, textile, and store operations"
};
---

<Base
  title="RFID Solutions for Retail & Textile | Altis Technology"
  description="RFID tag production, tunnel/box reading, store counting, inventory accuracy, and season turnover optimization solutions for retail and textile operations."
  {schema}
  lang="en"
  alternateUrl="https://www.altis.com.tr/sektorler/perakende-tekstil/"
>
<!-- Hero -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-grid-bg"></div>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <a href="/en/">Home</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <a href="/en/sectors/retail-textile/">Sectors</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <span style="color:var(--sector);font-weight:600">Retail &amp; Textile</span>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div>
        <div class="sector-pill">
          <span class="pill-tag">Sector</span>
          <span>Apparel · Retail · Distribution · Store</span>
        </div>
        <h1>From factory to store — every product, <em>traceable at every point.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">RFID is Altis's most mature solution area. Apparel and retail is the sector where Auto-ID technology can be applied with the highest efficiency. The Tag&amp;Trace platform, together with the RFID tunnels and boxes designed by Altis, builds a single traceability chain from the factory to the distribution center and on to the store shelf.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/en/contact/">Request a Retail Demo
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg" href="#use-cases">Explore Scenarios</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-platforms">
          <span class="lbl">Product used:</span>
          <a href="/en/platforms/tag-trace/" class="plat-chip">
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4"><path d="M4 11a9 9 0 0 1 9 9"/><path d="M4 4a16 16 0 0 1 16 16"/></svg>
            Tag&amp;Trace
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Hero visual: RFID journey -->
      <div class="retail-vis">
        <div class="retail-head">
          <div class="ttl">RFID Tracking · Brand X · Season SS-26</div>
          <div class="meta">
            <span class="live">live</span>
            <span>14,248 items</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="retail-body">
          <!-- Journey: Factory → DC → Store -->
          <div class="journey">
            <div class="journey-stage">
              <div class="ic">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="10" rx="1"/><path d="m6 11 6-7 6 7"/></svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lbl">Factory</div>
              <div class="nm">Production · Tagging</div>
              <div class="cnt">14,248 tags</div>
            </div>
            <div class="journey-stage">
              <div class="ic">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 9h18v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/><path d="M3 9 5 4h14l2 5"/></svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lbl">Distribution Center</div>
              <div class="nm">Shipment Verification</div>
              <div class="cnt">13,982 / 14,248</div>
            </div>
            <div class="journey-stage">
              <div class="ic">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 7h18v3a3 3 0 0 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1-6 0z"/><path d="M5 10v10h14V10"/></svg>
              </div>
              <div class="lbl">Store</div>
              <div class="nm">Stock &amp; Sales</div>
              <div class="cnt">in 8,412 stores</div>
            </div>
            <div class="journey-arrow a1">→</div>
            <div class="journey-arrow a2">→</div>
          </div>

          <!-- RFID stream -->
          <div class="rfid-stream">
            <div class="head">
              <span>Distribution Center Gate · Antenna DOOR-B</span>
              <span class="right">~3s / pallet · 2,700 tags / min</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tag-grid">
              <div class="tag-pill shipped"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill shipped"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill miss"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill shipped"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill shipped"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill shipped"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill miss"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill shipped"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill read"></div>
              <div class="tag-pill shipped"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="stream-stats">
              <span class="stat"><span class="dot s"></span>Read · 18</span>
              <span class="stat"><span class="dot o"></span>Shipped · 4</span>
              <span class="stat"><span class="dot x"></span>Missing · 2</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- KPIs -->
          <div class="retail-kpi-row">
            <div class="retail-kpi">
              <div class="l">Stock Accuracy</div>
              <div class="v ok">99.4%</div>
              <div class="meta">vs 92% last month</div>
            </div>
            <div class="retail-kpi">
              <div class="l">Season Turnover Speed</div>
              <div class="v s">×2.1</div>
              <div class="meta">vs previous season</div>
            </div>
            <div class="retail-kpi">
              <div class="l">Stock Loss</div>
              <div class="v ok">↓38%</div>
              <div class="meta">before vs. after RFID</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Pain points -->
<section class="pains">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead
      eyebrow="In Retail &amp; Textile"
      heading="Does this sound familiar?"
      description="Fast fashion, seasonal peaks, and the disconnect between store and warehouse make it constantly difficult to have the right stock in the right store. RFID is the only technology that eliminates this disconnect completely."
    />
    <div class="pain-grid" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="100">
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="qty">↓ 65%</div>
        <h3>Stock accuracy</h3>
        <p>Inventory counted manually or via barcode can't keep pace with fast-fashion turnover; actual store stock diverges from what the system shows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="qty">~ Hours</div>
        <h3>Slow counting</h3>
        <p>While store staff scan items one by one, closing hours stretch out; counts happen monthly instead of weekly, and problems are caught late.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="qty">∼ Invisible</div>
        <h3>Stock loss</h3>
        <p>Internal/external theft, mis-shipments, or recording errors — the discrepancy usually isn't detected until the next inventory count.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="qty">~ ↓ Turnover</div>
        <h3>Slow season turnover</h3>
        <p>When seasons change, product in the wrong location goes unsold and ends up discounted; the decision to transfer it to the right store comes too late.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Solution mapping -->
<section class="solution">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead
      eyebrow="Solution Map"
      heading="Apparel is the most mature use case for RFID"
      description="From product to shipment, from shipment to store shelf and POS, the entire chain is orchestrated through a single Auto-ID platform. Tag&amp;Trace is the layer at the center of that chain."
    />
    <div class="sol-map">
      <div class="sol-col">
        <h4>Need</h4>
        <div class="group">
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="9" width="18" height="9" rx="2"/><path d="M6 9V5h12v4"/></svg>RFID tag production &amp; printing</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/></svg>RFID tunnel &amp; box reading</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 9h18v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/><path d="M3 9 5 4h14l2 5"/></svg>DC shipment verification</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 7h18v3a3 3 0 0 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1-6 0z"/><path d="M5 10v10h14V10"/></svg>In-store counting</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="9" cy="12" r="4"/><circle cx="15" cy="12" r="4"/></svg>Loss prevention</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><ellipse cx="12" cy="6" rx="8" ry="3"/><path d="M4 6v12c0 1.7 3.6 3 8 3s8-1.3 8-3V6"/></svg>ERP &amp; WMS synchronization</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sol-col sol-platform">
        <div class="plat-card">
          <div class="nm">Tag&amp;Trace</div>
          <div class="role">RFID &amp; Auto-ID Orchestration Platform</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Reader, printer, antenna management · brand-agnostic</li>
            <li>Tag templates · EPC encoding · ZPL</li>
            <li>Visual rule engine · shipment verification</li>
            <li>ERP / WMS / SAP two-way integration</li>
            <li>Single operations center for store, DC, and factory</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sol-col">
        <h4>Result</h4>
        <div class="group">
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>99%+ stock accuracy</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>×20 counting speed</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>Faster season turnover</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>Significant drop in stock loss</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>Correct SKU distribution to stores</div>
          <div class="sol-tile"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>Faster POS &amp; return processing</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- RFID Hardware: Altis Tunnel + Box -->
<section class="hw">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="hw-grid" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="100">
      <div>
        <span class="badge">Altis Hardware</span>
        <h3>Altis-designed RFID tunnels and boxes</h3>
        <p>The backbone of our RFID Apparel and Retail solutions is the RFID tunnels and RFID boxes designed and manufactured by Altis Technology. These high-performance reading stations, capable of reading hundreds of tags at once in milliseconds, make the entire shipment-verification operation unmanned — from cartons on the production line to pallets at the distribution center.</p>
        <ul class="kv">
          <li>
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>
            <div>
              <strong>Ultra-fast reading</strong>
              Hundreds of RFID tags read at once, in milliseconds.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>
            <div>
              <strong>Enclosed-field reading</strong>
              Recognizes only the products inside the tunnel/box, with no leakage to the surroundings. No false tag reads.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>
            <div>
              <strong>Conveyor &amp; PLC integration</strong>
              Together with Tag&amp;Trace, conveyor speed control, line stopping, and PLC triggering are all managed from a single interface.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-11"/></svg>
            <div>
              <strong>EPC Gen2 &amp; SGTIN compliant</strong>
              Industry standard; works with your existing RFID tag infrastructure.
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tunnel-stage">
        <div class="tunnel-scene">
          <div class="tunnel">
            <div class="tunnel-frame">
              <div class="tunnel-label">RFID Tunnel · Altis</div>
              <div class="tunnel-antenna l1"></div>
              <div class="tunnel-antenna l2"></div>
              <div class="tunnel-antenna r1"></div>
              <div class="tunnel-antenna r2"></div>
              <div class="tunnel-carton">
                <div class="label">CARTON-04812</div>
                <div class="count">×64 SKU</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="tunnel-conveyor"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="tunnel-readings">
            <span class="epc active">E2 80 11 60</span>
            <span class="epc active">E2 80 11 62</span>
            <span class="epc">E2 80 11 65</span>
            <span class="epc active">E2 80 11 68</span>
            <span class="epc">E2 80 11 6A</span>
            <span class="epc active">+59</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tunnel-stats">
          <div class="tunnel-stat">
            <div class="l">Read time</div>
            <div class="v s">~120ms</div>
          </div>
          <div class="tunnel-stat">
            <div class="l">In carton</div>
            <div class="v">64 SKU</div>
          </div>
          <div class="tunnel-stat">
            <div class="l">Accuracy</div>
            <div class="v ok">100%</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Use cases -->
<section class="uc" id="use-cases">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead
      eyebrow="Retail &amp; Textile Scenarios"
      heading="6 actionable RFID solutions"
      description="Tag&amp;Trace and Altis RFID hardware are positioned as purpose-built applications at every point in the apparel chain."
    />
    <div class="uc-grid" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="100">
      <article class="uc-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="9" width="18" height="9" rx="2"/><path d="M6 9V5h12v4M6 18v2h12v-2"/></svg></div>
        <h3>RFID Tag Production</h3>
        <p>On the production line or at the tagging station, EPC-coded RFID tags are printed automatically using data from ERP/WMS and pass verification.</p>
        <div class="uc-impact">
          <div class="m"><div class="v">ZPL</div><div class="l">standard template</div></div>
          <div class="m"><div class="v">EPC</div><div class="l">automatic encoding</div></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="uc-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Tunnel / Box Reading</h3>
        <p>In Altis-designed RFID tunnels and boxes, every SKU inside a carton or pallet is identified in milliseconds. Verification at conveyor speed.</p>
        <div class="uc-impact">
          <div class="m"><div class="v">~120ms</div><div class="l">carton reading</div></div>
          <div class="m"><div class="v">100%</div><div class="l">accuracy</div></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="uc-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 9h18v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/><path d="M3 9 5 4h14l2 5"/></svg></div>
        <h3>DC Shipment Verification</h3>
        <p>At the distribution center, an RFID gate pass verifies every shipment's contents against the order. Product headed to the wrong store triggers an instant alert.</p>
        <div class="uc-impact">
          <div class="m"><div class="v">~3s</div><div class="l">pallet reading</div></div>
          <div class="m"><div class="v">Auto</div><div class="l">ERP confirmation</div></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="uc-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M3 7h18v3a3 3 0 0 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1-6 0 3 3 0 0 1-6 0z"/><path d="M5 10v10h14V10"/></svg></div>
        <h3>In-Store Counting</h3>
        <p>With a mobile RFID terminal, a single walk down the aisle counts the entire store inventory in minutes. Weekly or even daily counting becomes possible.</p>
        <div class="uc-impact">
          <div class="m"><div class="v">×20</div><div class="l">counting speed</div></div>
          <div class="m"><div class="v">99%+</div><div class="l">stock accuracy</div></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="uc-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></div>
        <h3>In-Store Item Location</h3>
        <p>Misplaced products or lost stock are found in seconds with a mobile terminal; staff can instantly answer "where is this item?"</p>
        <div class="uc-impact">
          <div class="m"><div class="v">RT</div><div class="l">live search</div></div>
          <div class="m"><div class="v">Auto</div><div class="l">location suggestion</div></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="uc-card">
        <div class="ic"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M20 7 12 3 4 7v10l8 4 8-4z"/><path d="M4 7l8 4 8-4M12 11v10"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Season Turnover Optimization</h3>
        <p>Live stock visibility across every store speeds up the transfer of unsold SKUs to the right location. End-of-season markdown loss goes down.</p>
        <div class="uc-impact">
          <div class="m"><div class="v">×2</div><div class="l">turnover speed</div></div>
          <div class="m"><div class="v">↓ Markdown</div><div class="l">loss</div></div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Operations flow -->
<section class="opflow">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead
      eyebrow="Supply Chain Flow"
      heading="From factory to store shelf, in five steps"
      description="The path a T-shirt takes from leaving the production line to reaching the store shelf. An RFID read at every step, a verified system record at every step."
    />
    <div class="op-steps">
      <div class="op-step">
        <div class="step-num">01</div>
        <h4>Production &amp; Tagging</h4>
        <p>At the end of the production line, an EPC-coded RFID tag is printed and applied to every product.</p>
        <span class="device">RFID Printer · ZPL</span>
      </div>
      <div class="op-step">
        <div class="step-num">02</div>
        <h4>Carton Verification</h4>
        <p>The Altis RFID tunnel/box reads every item inside in milliseconds; checks for anything missing.</p>
        <span class="device">RFID Tunnel · Box</span>
      </div>
      <div class="op-step">
        <div class="step-num">03</div>
        <h4>DC Shipment</h4>
        <p>Distribution center gate RFID antennas verify pallet-level shipments against the order.</p>
        <span class="device">RFID Gate · WMS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="op-step">
        <div class="step-num">04</div>
        <h4>Store Receiving</h4>
        <p>In the store back room, RFID readers bring incoming boxes into the system along with their contents.</p>
        <span class="device">Mobile RFID · POS</span>
      </div>
      <div class="op-step">
        <div class="step-num">05</div>
        <h4>Shelf &amp; Sale</h4>
        <p>In-store counting, product location search, and POS verification — one operation with mobile RFID.</p>
        <span class="device">Mobile RFID · POS</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ROI -->
<section class="roi">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead
      eyebrow="Expected Impact"
      heading="RFID-powered retail, measurable gains"
      description="Typical operational improvements observed in apparel and retail projects. Results vary based on product characteristics, store structure, and current operational maturity."
    />
    <div class="roi-grid" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="100">
      <div class="roi-card">
        <div class="b">99<sup>%+</sup></div>
        <div class="lbl">Stock accuracy</div>
        <div class="meta">Continuously verified inventory across store, DC, and production; ERP variance approaches zero.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="roi-card">
        <div class="b">×20<sup></sup></div>
        <div class="lbl">Counting speed</div>
        <div class="meta">Monthly counts become daily; stores no longer need to count during closed hours.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="roi-card">
        <div class="b">↓ 38<sup>%</sup></div>
        <div class="lbl">Stock loss</div>
        <div class="meta">Visible inventory and RFID gate control reduce internal/external loss and mis-shipments together.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="roi-card">
        <div class="b">×2<sup></sup></div>
        <div class="lbl">Season turnover speed</div>
        <div class="meta">Right product in the right store; end-of-season markdown loss drops noticeably.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Buyer FAQ -->
<section class="buyer">
  <div class="container">
    <SectionHead
      eyebrow="Which questions do we answer?"
      heading="By decision-maker profile"
      description="A retail RFID transformation is a team decision, not a single person's. Every role asks different questions; our answers speak clearly to each one."
    />
    <div class="buyer-grid" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="100">
      <div class="buyer-card">
        <span class="role-tag">Operations &amp; Store</span>
        <h3>How does it affect staff?</h3>
        <p class="q">"Will store staff have extra work to do? How long is the training? Will it disrupt our existing POS?"</p>
        <div class="ans">Field operations work with familiar workflows; the mobile RFID terminal closely resembles a handheld barcode scanner. Training takes 1-2 days; it can start with a pilot store and scale to the full chain. POS stays the same and is integrated for verification.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="buyer-card">
        <span class="role-tag">IT &amp; Digital</span>
        <h3>How does it fit our existing systems?</h3>
        <p class="q">"We don't want to replace our WMS / ERP / SAP. Does it meet our security standards?"</p>
        <div class="ans">Tag&amp;Trace steps in as an orchestration layer, leaving existing systems in place. Two-way communication over REST, MQTT, and OPC UA, token-based security, RBAC, and audit logs are all standard.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="buyer-card">
        <span class="role-tag">General Manager / CFO</span>
        <h3>What's the return on investment?</h3>
        <p class="q">"Does tag cost eat into product margin? How long does a pilot take? Which metrics are used to measure it?"</p>
        <div class="ans">Apparel RFID tag costs have fallen to a negligible percentage of product margin. Pilots run 3-6 months; counting speed, stock accuracy, stock loss, and turnover speed are measured before and after. Typical payback is 12-18 months.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

